{"id": "section-body-04173", "title": "Influenza", "chapterId": "chapter-four", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "NOTIFIABLE DISEASES", "Viral Infections", "Influenza"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-04173", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Influenza", "runs": [{"text": "Influenza"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1802"}}, {"id": "body-04174", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Influenza is an acute respiratory viral infection caused by influenza viruses and readily spread from person to person, via infectious respiratory particles (IRP), which are transmitted through the air when an infected person coughs or sneezes. There are four types of influenza viruses: types A, B, C and D. Seasonal influenza A and B viruses circulate among humans worldwide. However, a novel influenza A virus’s subtypes of animal origin (zoonotic influenza), such as avian influenza A virus and swine influenza A virus can sporadically affect humans and are known to cause pandemics.", "runs": [{"text": "Influenza is an acute respiratory viral infection caused by influenza viruses and readily spread from person to person, via infectious"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "respiratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "particles"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IRP),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "transmitted"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "through"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "air"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "when"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "person"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "coughs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sneezes."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "There are four types of influenza viruses: types A, B, C and D. Seasonal influenza A and B viruses circulate among humans worldwide."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "However,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "novel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus’s"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "subtypes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "animal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "origin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(zoonotic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza),"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "such"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "avian"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus and swine influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus can sporadically affect humans and are known to cause pandemics."}]}, {"id": "body-04175", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Influenza A viruses are further classified into subtypes according to the combinations of the proteins H for Hemagglutinin and N for Neuraminidase on the surface of the virus (e.g., H1N1, H5N1, H3N2, etc.)", "runs": [{"text": "Influenza A viruses are further classified into subtypes according to the combinations of the proteins H for Hemagglutinin and N for Neuraminidase on the surface of the virus (e.g., H1N1, H5N1, H3N2, etc.)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04176", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Influenza B viruses are not classified into subtypes but can be subclassified into two lineages. Currently circulating influenza type B viruses belong to either the B/Yamagata or B/Victoria lineages.", "runs": [{"text": "Influenza B viruses are not classified into subtypes but can be subclassified into two lineages. Currently circulating influenza type B viruses belong to either the B/Yamagata or B/Victoria lineages."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04178", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04179", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Clinical diagnosis of influenza is challenging as the signs and symptoms of the disease can be non-specific (many respiratory pathogens can cause a similar illness) and can vary depending on virus type as well as patient host characteristics and other factors. Most people with non-severe influenza illness recover from the fever and other symptoms within a week, without requiring medical attention. Typically ranges from 2 to 7 days, though it can extend to 10 days for some subtypes (e.g., H5N1). Symptoms: fever, sudden onset of cough, headache, muscle and joint pain, severe malaise, sore throat, rhinorrhea, chills and sweating", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "diagnosis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "challenging"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "signs"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "symptoms"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "non-specific"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(many"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "respiratory pathogens"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cause"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "similar"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "illness)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vary"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "depending"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "type"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "well"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "host"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "characteristics"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "other factors. Most people with non-severe influenza illness recover from the fever and other symptoms within a week, without requiring"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "medical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "attention."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Typically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ranges"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "from"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "2"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "7"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "though"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "extend"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "10"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "days"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "some"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "subtypes"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "H5N1). Symptoms:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sudden"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "onset"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cough,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "headache,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "muscle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "joint"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pain,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "malaise,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sore"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "throat,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rhinorrhea,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chills"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and "}, {"text": "sweating"}]}, {"id": "body-04181", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Signs: elevated body temperature, pharyngeal erythema, nasal congestion or discharge, cervical lymphadenopathy, lung wheezing or crackles if complications like pneumonia develop, tachycardia and general appearance of malaise or fatigue", "runs": [{"text": "Signs: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "elevated body temperature, pharyngeal erythema, nasal congestion or discharge, cervical lymphadenopathy, lung wheezing or crackles if complications like pneumonia develop, tachycardia and general appearance of malaise or fatigue"}]}, {"id": "body-04183", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Complications: septicemia, septic shock, severe pneumonia, acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS), multi-organ failure, exacerbation of chronic medical conditions or even death.", "runs": [{"text": "Complications: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "septicemia, septic shock, severe pneumonia, acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS), multi-organ failure, exacerbation of chronic medical conditions or even death."}]}, {"id": "body-04185", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Case Definitions", "runs": [{"text": "Case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Definitions"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04186", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Suspected case: Any person presenting with unexplained acute lower respiratory illness with fever (>38 ºC) and cough, sore throat, shortness of breath or difficulty breathing AND at least one of the following exposures within the 7 days prior to", "runs": [{"text": "Suspected case:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Any person presenting with unexplained acute lower respiratory illness with fever (>38 ºC) and cough, sore throat, shortness of breath or difficulty breathing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "AND at least one of the following exposures within the 7 days prior to"}]}, {"id": "body-04187", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Infected animals (e.g., poultry, swine, or wild birds) or their environments (e.g., live animal markets, farms, or slaughterhouses).", "runs": [{"text": "Infected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "animals"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "poultry,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "swine,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "wild"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "birds)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "their"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "environments"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "live"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "animal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "markets,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "farms,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or "}, {"text": "slaughterhouses)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04188", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "A confirmed human case of zoonotic influenza.", "runs": [{"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirmed"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "human"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "zoonotic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04190", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Probable Case: A suspected case with:", "runs": [{"text": "Probable", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Case:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with:"}]}, {"id": "body-04191", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "A positive laboratory test for influenza A, but the subtype is not identified or is inconclusive (e.g., influenza A positive but not H1N1, H3N2, or other common human subtypes).", "runs": [{"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "positive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "test"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "but"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "subtype"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "identified"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inconclusive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "positive but not H1N1, H3N2, or other common human subtypes)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04192", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Epidemiological evidence strongly suggesting zoonotic exposure (e.g., direct contact with infected animals or their products).", "runs": [{"text": "Epidemiological evidence strongly suggesting zoonotic exposure (e.g., direct contact with infected animals or their "}, {"text": "products)."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04193", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "No definitive confirmation of a novel influenza A subtype.", "runs": [{"text": "No"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "definitive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirmation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "novel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "subtype."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04195", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Confirmed Case: A suspected or probable case with:", "runs": [{"text": "Confirmed", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Case:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suspected"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "probable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with:"}]}, {"id": "body-04196", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Laboratory confirmation of infection with a novel influenza A virus of animal origin, such as:", "runs": [{"text": "Laboratory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirmation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "novel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "animal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "origin,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "such"}, {"text": " as:"}]}, {"id": "body-04197", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Detection of a specific novel influenza A subtype (e.g., H5N1, H7N9, H3N2v) by reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR) or other nucleic acid amplification tests.", "runs": [{"text": "Detection of a specific novel influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "subtype (e.g., H5N1, H7N9, H3N2v) by reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR) or other nucleic acid amplification tests."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04198", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Virus isolation or sequencing confirming a novel influenza A virus not typically found in humans.", "runs": [{"text": "Virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "isolation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sequencing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "confirming"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "novel"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "influenza"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "virus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "typically"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "found"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "humans."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1767"}}, {"id": "body-04199", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Significant rise in subtype-specific antibodies (e.g., via serologic testing like hemagglutination inhibition or microneutralization assays).", "runs": [{"text": "Significant"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "rise"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "subtype-specific"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "antibodies"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(e.g.,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "via"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "serologic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "testing"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "like"}, {"text"